# repos-manager

> {{ site.description }}

repos-manager is a single native binary written in Rust, for Linux, macOS and Windows (x86_64 and ARM64). It asks each forge for every repository you can access (your own, your organizations and the projects you collaborate on) and mirrors them locally as `<base_dir>/<host>/<owner>/<repo>`, cloning what is missing and fast-forwarding the rest. Dirty working copies are never touched. At runtime it only needs `git` and the official CLI of each forge you use (`gh`, `glab`, `tea`, `bitbucket`, `rad`).

Typical session:

```sh
curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dxsk/repos-manager/main/installers/install.sh | sh
repos-manager login         # log in to every installed forge CLI
repos-manager sync --all    # clone and update everything
repos-manager status        # dirty, ahead, behind and diverged repos
```

